{
  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "The best configuration so far is config_033 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted + multiprofile) at 0.7250 accuracy and only 3.60 GPU hours. All other dimensions (image encoder, aggregation, fusion, profile) have been well-characterized and point clearly to vit_l + transformer + weighted + multiprofile. The one remaining untested dimension in this top-performing setup is the RNA encoder: pca_n2000. config_011 tests whether a simpler linear PCA encoder can match or exceed the learned scvi_n200 encoder when paired with the strongest image/aggregation/fusion stack. If pca_n2000 performs comparably, it would offer a cheaper alternative (no variational autoencoder training); if it underperforms, it confirms scvi_n200 as the optimal RNA encoder and locks in the best configuration with 2 experiments remaining for final validation or minor tuning. Expected cost is similar to or slightly below config_033 (~3–3.5 GPU hours) since PCA is a lightweight linear projection replacing the scvi encoder, while the vit_l + transformer + multiprofile pipeline dominates training time."
}

